+[[custom-collection-implementations]]
+==== Custom collection implementation types
+
+The concrete types in the table can be replaced with entries in a `mapstruct.properties` resource at the root of the mapping compilation classpath:
+
+[source, properties]
+----
+mapstruct.collectionImplementation.java.util.List=com.example.CustomList
+mapstruct.collectionImplementation.java.util.Map=com.example.CustomMap
+----
+
+The `mapstruct.configurationFile` annotation processor option selects a different resource by relative path on that same classpath.
+An explicitly selected resource must exist; if the default `mapstruct.properties` resource is absent, MapStruct uses the built-in implementations.
+
+The configured class must be public, concrete, assignable to the configured interface, preserve its unbounded type parameters, and provide a public no-argument constructor that declares no checked exceptions.
+If it also provides a usable public `int` constructor, MapStruct passes the source size as the initial capacity.
+Object factories still take precedence over configured implementations.
